# The published repository is the deployment: the package's runtime modules,
# its entry point, the Vercel config, the runtime requirements, the fitted model
# and four runtime tables. Everything else -- what a clone would use to test,
# lint, retrain, collect or run elsewhere -- stays on this machine.
#
# Check after changing this file: `git add -A --dry-run` must list only the
# publish set, and tests/test_stateless.py asserts what must and must not ship.

# --- Generated by tools --------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
# Written by the Vercel CLI if it is ever linked here; names the account's
# project and team.
.vercel/

# --- Secrets and machine-specific configuration ----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# Generated by scripts/schedule_macos.sh for this machine: it holds absolute
# paths under the home directory of whoever ran it.
com.phishing_detector.collect.plist

# --- Local data ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feed snapshots, the evidence cache (raw pages from scanned sites), and the
# corpus: the 1.4 GB database and collector output.
data/snapshots/
data/cache/
data/corpus/*
# Four files under it are runtime inputs the model was fitted alongside -- the
# brand lists, the favicon hash table and the Public Suffix List every mode
# reads (urls.PSL_FILE). A clone without them scores with a seed list, no
# favicon matching and a stale suffix list, silently. They ship.
!data/corpus/brands.json
!data/corpus/favicon_hashes.json
!data/corpus/brand_regional.json
!data/corpus/public_suffix_list.dat
# The training table and its superseded copies, measurement results, and the
# logs the scheduled collector and other scripts append to (tracking those would
# dirty the tree on a timer).
data/*.csv
data/*.json
data/*.log
data/collect.err
# The fitted model under models/ ships: 42 MB, nearly all of it the bootstrap
# ensemble, and a deployment that pulls from the repository has no other way to
# get it.

# --- Offline code: training, data collection, review tools ---------------------
# Measured 2026-10-07: the running site never imports these (a full scan, result,
# no-script and history pass loaded every other module, and no runtime module
# imports them, even lazily).
src/phishing_detector/data/asn_enrich.py
src/phishing_detector/data/benign_hosting.py
src/phishing_detector/data/collect.py
src/phishing_detector/data/commoncrawl.py
src/phishing_detector/data/feeds.py
src/phishing_detector/data/login_pages.py
src/phishing_detector/feedback_cli.py
src/phishing_detector/model/baseline.py
src/phishing_detector/model/dataset.py
src/phishing_detector/model/preprocess.py
tests/
scripts/

# --- Development and local running ---------------------------------------------
docs/
deploy/
Makefile
package.json
ruff.toml
requirements-dev.txt
# Local containment only: nothing published depends on them, and the public
# deployment does not use a container.
Dockerfile
compose.yaml
.dockerignore
/*.png
